  <!-- operation: create -->
  <xs:complexType name="op_create" mixed="true">
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string" use="required" fixed="create"/>
    <xs:attribute name="value" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
  </xs:complexType>

  <!-- operation: database -->
  <xs:complexType name="op_database">
    <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:element name="acl" type="op_database__acl" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The acl (Access Control List) instruction contains information about access rights. Its attributes define which rights its child-elements will receive.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="$document"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;acl read="true" write="false" delete="false" changeACL="false"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;user group="{$groupid}"&gt;{$userid}&lt;/user&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;group&gt;{$groupid}&lt;/group&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;/acl&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="attach" type="op_database__attach" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The attach instruction is used to attach streams to Objects. It has two attributes to and slot.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="https://xios3.com/image.jpg"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;attach to="home://myFile.xml" slot="2"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="copy" type="op_database__copy" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The copy instruction is used to copy Objects and Containers and has two attributes, to and silent. The to attribute is a string type attribute, and is used to define the destination Container.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="home://Documents/MyDocument.xml"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;copy to="home://Applications/" silent="false"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="create" type="op_database__create" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Instruction of the database, groups operations.</p><p>In database: The create instruction is used to create Objects or Containers and has two attributes, type and name.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="home://Documents/"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;create type="container" name="Contactbook"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;content&gt;Contact&lt;/content&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;/create&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre><p>In groups: Using the create instruction we can create new groups for different access-rights across applications or data The attribute value controls which parent-group is being used.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="tenant"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;create type="subgroup" name="{$groupName}" alias="{$groupAlias}" public="public" applicant="open" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="delete" type="op_database__delete" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Instruction of the change, database, groups operations.</p><p>In change: Deleting data is done by either deleting the current selection of a component or by supplying an XPath expression in the select attribute.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="change" value="home://Documents/"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;delete select="/db:result/db:object[@name='{$fileTitle}']"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre><p>In database: The delete instruction is used to delete Objects and Containers and has two attributes, permanent and silent, both which are boolean type attributes.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="home://Documents/MyDocument.xml"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;delete permanent="true" silent="false"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre><p>In groups: Deletes a group, role, or subgroup to a group.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$pathToGroup"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;delete type="group" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="detach" type="op_database__detach" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The detach instruction is used to detach attachments from Objects. It has only one attribute slot which is a numeric type attribute and defines the attachment slot to remove.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="home://Documents/myFile.xml"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;detach slot="3"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="link" type="op_database__link" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The link instruction is used to access Objects through a link for a certain amount of time from the CloudBackend database. Its termination can be specified through a max amount of downloads or a duration given in days, hours and minutes.</p>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="listen" type="op_database__listen" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The listen instruction is used to listen to changes made in a Container or a document. The Object to listen to is defined in the value attribute of the operation element.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="home://Documents/"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;listen event="Append" step="newFile"/&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;listen event="Remove" step="deleteFile"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="mount" type="op_database__mount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The mount instruction is used to mount a new database similarily to how channel sets up a new communication channel. The difference is that a new database uses an already established communication channel.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;mount name="my-mount" hidden="false"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;group path="tenant/myGroup"/&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;/mount&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="move" type="op_database__move" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Instruction of the change, database operations.</p><p>In change: Moves an XML node-set from one part of the document to another part</p><p>In database: The move instruction is used to move Objects and Containers and has two attributes, to and silent.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="home://Documents/MyDocument.xml"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;move to="home://Applications/" silent="true"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="publish" type="op_database__publish" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The publish instruction creates a new publication of a selection of Objects or Containers that may be externally accessed from the database without any authentication. Note: Publications can be found under main://.published or under a group, tenant://Groups/.published.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;publish suggest="{$nameSuggest}" id="{$trigger#@id}" alias="newUniqueName" exists="alreadyExists"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="rename" type="op_database__rename" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Instruction of the database, groups operations.</p><p>In database: The rename instruction is used to rename Objects and Containers.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="home://document1.xml"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;rename to="document_hello.xml"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre><p>In groups: Instruction to rename a role, group or the current users alias within the specified group.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$groupPath"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;rename name="Cool Bob" type="role" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="restore" type="op_database__restore" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The restore instruction restores previous versions of Objects or Containers that have been permanently deleted (when a Trashcan has not been used). It requires the Container-path where the Object/Container is located and the corresponding id.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="$containerPath"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;restore id="$objectId" name="new restored name.xml" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="share" type="op_database__share" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The share instruction is used to share Objects, documents, photos, and Containers with friends. Any Object or container which the user has created in the database can be selected to be shared.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="#view1#gridFilesToShare"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;share use-selection="true"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;users&gt;{#view1#gridSelectedFriends}&lt;/users&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;comment&gt;{#view1#commentInputfield}&lt;/comment&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;/share&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="shares" type="op_database__shares" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The shares instruction lists all shares from a whole group or a group filtered by a specific user. Note: The currently logged in users personal shares are instead available here main://.shares.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;shares id="{$groupid}:{$userid}" alias="bob"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="shortcut" type="op_database__shortcut" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The shortcut instruction allows you to add a shortcut. It has the following attributes "to","name" and"alias", allowing you to define which Container the shortcut should appear in, what its name will be and what its internal reference alias will be, respectively.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="!"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;shortcut to="{$atomFeed}" name="{#shortcutwizard#name}" alias="title"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;icon&gt;{$shortcutIcon}&lt;/icon&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;target&gt;{#shortcutwizard#location}&lt;/target&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;data&gt;&lt;/data&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;startfolder&gt;&lt;/startfolder&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;/shortcut&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="subscribe" type="op_database__subscribe" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The subscribe instruction is used to add a publication to your subscribed publications (published by other identities). This allows the logged in identity to subscribe to data being added, deleted, or modified in a published Container.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;subscribe name="Vacation 2024" userid="12884901892" id="4" password="test"/&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;subscribe name="Vacation 2024" username="test4" password="test"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="subscribers" type="op_database__subscribers" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The subscribers instruction is used to receive a db:result Object that lists all subscribers of a specified publication by the currently logged in identity or a group that the identity has got access to.…</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;subscribers id="123" alias="MySubscribers"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="trashcan" type="op_database__trashcan" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The trashcan instruction is used to deal with the system trashcan. The value attribute is used for two different purposes depending on the value in the action attribute.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="xios"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;trashcan action="empty" silent="false"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="truncate" type="op_database__truncate" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The truncate operation handles a fast and easy way to, well, empty a Container. There are two attributes to let you chose in which fasion the emptying is done.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="{$pathToEmpty}"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;truncate silent="false" progress="true"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="unlink" type="op_database__unlink" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The unlink instruction is used to unlink published Objects or Containers links.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;unlink id="{#names#name1}"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="unlisten" type="op_database__unlisten" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The unlisten instruction is used to remove an Object or Container listener (see above). The Object to remove the listener from is defined in the value attribute of the operation element.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="home://Documents/"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;unlisten event="FileAdded"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="unpublish" type="op_database__unpublish" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The unpublish instruction allows you to remove a previously created publish (publication). Note: Publications can be found under main://.published or under a group, tenant://Groups/.published.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;unpublish id="{$publishId}"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="unshare" type="op_database__unshare" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The unshare instruction is used to unshare Objects or Containers that are already shared.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;unshare&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;packages&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;package id="{$shareId}"/&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;/packages&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;/unshare&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="unsubscribe" type="op_database__unsubscribe" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The subscribe instruction is used to remove a publication from the currently logged in identity subscriptions. Note: Subscriptions for the currently logged in identity can be found under main://.subscribed, a group can not subscribe to a publication and does not have this object.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;unsubscribe id="4" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="upload" type="op_database__upload" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The upload instruction is used to upload Objects to a destination Container. It has only one attribute to which is a string type attribute and defines the destination Container.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;upload to="home://Documents/"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="unmount" type="op__leaf" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The unmount instruction is used to unmount mounted database drives.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;unmount name="example"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:choice>
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string" use="required" fixed="database"/>
    <xs:attribute name="value" type="xs:string"/>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:complexType name="op_database__acl">
    <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:element name="user" type="op_database__acl__user" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
      <xs:element name="group" type="op_database__acl__group" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
    </xs:choice>
    <xs:attribute name="read" type="xs:boolean" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="write" type="xs:boolean" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="delete" type="xs:boolean" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="changeACL" type="xs:boolean" use="required"/>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:complexType name="op_database__acl__user">
    <xs:sequence minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:any namespace="##any" processContents="skip"/>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:complexType name="op_database__acl__group">
    <xs:sequence minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:any namespace="##any" processContents="skip"/>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:complexType name="op_database__attach">
    <xs:sequence minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:any namespace="##any" processContents="skip"/>
    </xs:sequence>
    <xs:attribute name="to" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="slot" type="xs:string"/>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:complexType name="op_database__copy">
    <xs:sequence minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:any namespace="##any" processContents="skip"/>
    </xs:sequence>
    <xs:attribute name="to" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
    <xs:attribute name="silent" type="xs:boolean"/>
  </xs:complexType>
  <xs:complexType name="op_database__create">
    <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:element name="author" type="op_database__create__author" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
      <xs:element name="summary" type="op_database__create__summary" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
      <xs:element name="acl" type="op_database__create__acl" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The acl (Access Control List) instruction contains information about access rights. Its attributes define which rights its child-elements will receive.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="$document"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;acl read="true" write="false" delete="false" changeACL="false"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;user group="{$groupid}"&gt;{$userid}&lt;/user&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;group&gt;{$groupid}&lt;/group&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;/acl&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="index" type="op_database__create__index" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
