  </xs:complexType>

  <!-- operation: groups -->
  <xs:complexType name="op_groups">
    <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:element name="accept" type="op_groups__accept" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Allows a user to accept an invitation to a group.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;accept to="home://Groups/{$group}"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="acceptRequest" type="op_groups__acceptRequest" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Accepting a request to join a group, where the parent value points to the team</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$groupPath"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;acceptRequest id="{$groupid}" reason="{$reason}" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="add" type="op_groups__add" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Instruction to add a role to the given group via the value-attribute</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$groupPath"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;add name="{$username}" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="addAvatar" type="op_groups__addAvatar" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The addAvatar instruction is used to save a group specific avatar for the user. This instruction also uses the value attribute of the operation element to define the URL to the image, which to use.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="{$dropSrc}"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;addAvatar to="xios" left="0" top="0" width="128" height="128"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="ban" type="op_groups__ban" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Bans a user from a group and sends a comment/reason as to why the user has been banned.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="tenant"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;ban name="bob1337" reason="to many bobs" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="create" type="op_groups__create" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Instruction of the database, groups operations.</p><p>In database: The create instruction is used to create Objects or Containers and has two attributes, type and name.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="home://Documents/"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;create type="container" name="Contactbook"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;content&gt;Contact&lt;/content&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;/create&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre><p>In groups: Using the create instruction we can create new groups for different access-rights across applications or data The attribute value controls which parent-group is being used.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="tenant"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;create type="subgroup" name="{$groupName}" alias="{$groupAlias}" public="public" applicant="open" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="delete" type="op_groups__delete" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Instruction of the change, database, groups operations.</p><p>In change: Deleting data is done by either deleting the current selection of a component or by supplying an XPath expression in the select attribute.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="change" value="home://Documents/"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;delete select="/db:result/db:object[@name='{$fileTitle}']"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre><p>In database: The delete instruction is used to delete Objects and Containers and has two attributes, permanent and silent, both which are boolean type attributes.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="database" value="home://Documents/MyDocument.xml"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;delete permanent="true" silent="false"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre><p>In groups: Deletes a group, role, or subgroup to a group.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$pathToGroup"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;delete type="group" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="deleteAvatar" type="op_groups__deleteAvatar" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>This instruction is used to delete the current avatar for a specific group. It does not utilize the value attribute.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="{$dropSrc}"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;deleteAvatar to="xios"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="invite" type="op_groups__invite" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Invite user/users to a group.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="tenant/mygroup"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;invite&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&#32;&#32;&lt;message&gt;Hello!&lt;/message&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;/invite&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="join" type="op_groups__join" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Using the join instruction lets you join a group upon an invite.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;join to="{$groupid}" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="kick" type="op_groups__kick" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>Kick a group member.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="group"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;kick name="{$user}" reason="&lt;/3" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="reject" type="op__leaf" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>This instruction answers to an invitation with a rejection, with a given reason.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$groupPath"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;reject id="$userid" reason="I must find my own way..." /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="request" type="op__leaf" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>This instruction allows you to send a request as the current user to join a specified group. Value defines which group to join.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$groupPath"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;request name="bobert" reason="party pls" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="saveMeta" type="op__leaf" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The saveMeta instruction extracts meta data from a document named profile.xml in the group database. Works only on main group.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$channelName"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;saveMeta/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="status" type="op__leaf" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The status instruction sets the users status message and online status within the specified group.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$groupPath"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;status message="having a good day"&gt;available&lt;/status&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="unban" type="op__leaf" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The unban instruction relieves a user from a prior ban in the specified group.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$groupPath"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;unban reason="Good bob" name="bobert" /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="leave" type="op__leaf" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>The leave instruction is used to leave the specified group as the current user. To specify which group the value attribute is set on the operation element.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="$groupPath"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;leave /&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="list" type="op__leaf" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:annotation><xs:documentation xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[<p>By using the list operation we can retrieve information about groups in a list. The list operation can list the group members, banned users, applicants, invites, and roles of a group.</p><pre><code>&lt;operation name="groups" value="tenant"&gt;<br/>&#32;&#32;&lt;list type="groupMembers" offset="100" count="200" responseAlias="listResponse"/&gt;<br/>&lt;/operation&gt;</code></pre>]]></xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:choice>
    <xs:attribute name="name" type="xs:string" use="required" fixed="groups"/>
    <xs:attribute name="value" type="xs:string" use="required"/>
  </xs:complexType>
